{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges","id":935535,"title":"Handeling Social/Mental Challenges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-22T05:27:42-07:00","id":935535,"title":"Handeling Social/Mental Challenges","content":"Hi everyone, just wanted your oppinions/advice on how to handle scenes where there is a big difference between the characters stats and the players stats. In my experience, in a physical challenge (fight/whatever) dice are rolled to determine the outcome but in most social situations and some mental (riddles for example) it's all down to how good a roleplayer you are and what your social and mental capabilities are.<br /> This might come from the fact that my usual ST is mostly used to Nordic style LARPing, letting the person instead of the dice do the talking.<br /> So how do you deal with a player who has a very socially capable character (high Charisma, Manipulations, Wits, Subterfuge, etc.) but isn't that good in social situation IRL. Or the other way around, a player who is good in social situations but plays characters with 1 or 2 in social stats? Or a &quot;stupid&quot; player trying to play a genius character. Or a highly intelligent (or even medium intelligent) player trying to play a &quot;stupid&quot; character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T13:20:17-07:00","id":935767,"title":"","content":"I go more by their CHARACTER's stats, modified by how good/well they RP.. That way those social/mental stats don't just become meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T12:49:34-07:00","id":936195,"title":"","content":"How would you feel about the following; a character is engaged in a social challenge, player talks the talk etc and at the end rolls whatever is appropriate, the difficulty of the roll is determined by how well the ST thinks the player did on his own with a poor performance giving a higher difficulty on the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:52:41-07:00","id":936259,"title":"","content":"That is what i was saying. You still roll, but modify it by how well (or poorly) he rps it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:21:41-07:00","id":936335,"title":"","content":"I always start with the roleplaying. That's one of the major reasons our group plays, so if it makes for an interesting scene, the dice take a backseat.<br /> <br /> If there's a real disparity between player ability and character stats, I'll abstract it out. <br /> <br /> &quot;What do you want to accomplish with this conversation/interaction?&quot;<br /> <br /> Then we'll roll, modified for circumstances - if I know a player has a character with high Manipulation, Perception, Wits, Subturfuge or Politics, I'll give them some ideas on how they can leverage the situation before the roll so they can adapt their approach. If the player has a great idea but their character doesn't really have the savvy to pull it off, I'll allow it but I may ask for some justification for why a socially awkward character knows just what to do in this situation.<br /> <br /> The result of the roll determines how well player approached the situation. 3 successes net means they got what they were after. 2 means they had to make a minor concession but still got it. 1 success means they got it but maybe not in the way they were expecting. <br /> <br /> Then we go on to narrarate the scene how it plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:33:14-07:00","id":936342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges?p=936335#post936335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always start with the roleplaying. That's one of the major reasons our group plays, so if it makes for an interesting scene, the dice take a backseat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've known a lot more people who were smarter, more glib etc than their characters ever were, so unless there are other mechanical reasons to have/keep those stats, if you are just going to default to Their skill vice their characters, what exacly is the point in keeping those stats?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:45:41-07:00","id":936352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges?p=936342#post936342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've known a lot more people who were smarter, more glib etc than their characters ever were, so unless there are other mechanical reasons to have/keep those stats, if you are just going to default to Their skill vice their characters, what exacly is the point in keeping those stats?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Easy. They can't read my mind. So if they want the level of insight into a situation that goes beyond the surface of what I'm portrayig as an NPC they're going to need to give me Wits + Empathy rolls, or such. If they say something that would trigger a specific reaction, I might make them roll to catch it, otherwise I omit that reaction or play it down. These rolls are alsi vital if you don't want to give away your motives or risk exposing your plans to scrutiny. <br /> <br /> My point is the rolls are secondary to the narrative. An ST can tailor an interaction or &quot;tactical&quot; situation to a player's stats if everyone is on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T02:57:22-07:00","id":936989,"title":"","content":"Erm, you could use the social combat rules from Dead Man's Party, and a Mental traits equivalent for battles of the mind. Easy peasy. <br /> <br /> The same system could be adapted for mental combat, but instead of Favour, Disfavour, etc, I'd just establish a successes threshold with the first character past the post winning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-25-2016, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T03:16:35-07:00","id":936992,"title":"","content":"True but i still want the essence of roleplay there. I don't want to turn everything into rollplaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:14:43-07:00","id":937242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges?p=936992#post936992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but i still want the essence of roleplay there. I don't want to turn everything into rollplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>But at what point does role playing, override skills/attributes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T18:40:56-07:00","id":937395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges?p=937242#post937242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But at what point does role playing, override skills/attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it makes for a better story is the best answer I can give. It's highly subjective and kind of a wishy-washy answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T22:13:42-07:00","id":937483,"title":"","content":"My thing though, is you eventually can get to a point of &quot;why even have those stats' then..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:15:04-07:00","id":938606,"title":"","content":"I disagree. You should role play and then roll for important encounters. A player should not get a roll unless they rp the social conflict, just like they should not get a combat roll unless they tell you what they are doing exactly. And rp should not do anything more than modify the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:07:00-07:00","id":938811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges?p=938606#post938606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. You should role play and then roll for important encounters. A player should not get a roll unless they rp the social conflict, just like they should not get a combat roll unless they tell you what they are doing exactly. And rp should not do anything more than modify the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you do not act out a combat scene in the same way that you act out a social scene. Sure it is more preferable if the player is more descritive than &quot;i hit the enemy with my sword&quot; or &quot;i shoot him in the face&quot;.<br /> But can't the same type of description work with a social roll as well. Something like &quot;I attempt to persuade the Prince in order to get him to do this (insert goal). I appeal to his sense of honor and justice&quot; or &quot;I attempt to intimidate the policeofficer by reminding him of the kickbacks he's taken from me in the past and by explaining to him that he's family would be safer if he does what i ask of him&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:21:19-07:00","id":938818,"title":"","content":"If you are engaging in combat in my games, you have to do more than &quot;I shoot him in the face&quot; to allow a combat roll in my games. Something like &quot;Raising my .45 Magnum with both my hands, my left hand bracing my right hand, I aim my pistol at his face and fire.&quot; That would be enough for me to allow a combat roll and, robably, to give a +1 bonus to die pool for the player.<br /> <br /> Saying that &quot;I attempt to persuade the Prince in order to get him to do this 'X'&quot; would not allow a social roll in my games. Something like &quot;Your Grace, you are known for your sense of justify and honor through the Courts of North America, I appeal to you, as a noble scion of 'X' Clan, please grant me a boon. If you will not help me, who will help me?&quot;. That would be enough for me to allow a social roll and, probably, to give a +1 bonus to die pool for the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:07:29-07:00","id":940561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/935535-handeling-social-mental-challenges?p=936992#post936992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but i still want the essence of roleplay there. I don't want to turn everything into rollplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you said we're dealing with characters whose social or mental traits may not be equal to those of the player (either higher or lower). So you *can't* always act out a scene in such circumstances. That's why social combat exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}